; test-commitment - the commitment and witness layout, driven end to end
;
; The first spend-shaped exercise of the witness model: a bll program
; committed as the body of a taproot leaf under the bll leaf version
; 0xc2, spent through the repl's spend command, which validates the
; real transaction instead of trusting four separately set context
; pieces. What the other corpus examples assume, this one checks:
;
;   - the executing program is the committed leaf script, so (tx 6)
;     is the hash of the program that actually runs
;   - the witness stack after the optional annex is exactly the
;     environment element, the leaf script and the control block
;   - the environment and the leaf script are canonically encoded,
;     one unique serialization each, and a redundant encoding refuses
;   - the budget is bought by the input's serialized witness bytes
;   - the verdict is the acceptance predicate: a truthy result is
;     valid, an error, a nil result or an exhausted budget is not
;
; The committed program is the simplest real contract, a
; pay-to-pubkey:
;
;   (bip340_verify (q . 0x754e3239f325570cdbbf4a87deee8a66b7f2b33479d468fbc1a50743bf56cc18) (bip342_txmsg) 1)
;
; The pubkey constant is quoted inside the committed program, so the
; taproot commitment binds it with no further rule. That binding is
; the property the singleton port's GENESIS and INNER arguments are
; waiting on, restored by committing constants in the program body
; rather than passing them as witness arguments.
;
; The signature message commits to the executing leaf: bip342_txmsg
; takes the leaf version from the control block, so context A's
; signature is over a message naming the same tapleaf hash (tx 6)
; returns, and no tapscript path could share it. The oracle
; originally hardcoded tapscript's version here, fixed in this unit
; (decided 2026-07-18, Evan) and pinned by the sighash case in
; test-spend.py.
;
; All hex constants below were produced by
;   python3 examples/gen-test-context.py commitment
; The committed leaf script is
;   ff26ffff80a0754e3239f325570cdbbf4a87deee8a66b7f2b33479d468fbc1a50743bf56cc18ffff2a80ff0180
; and its 0xc2 tapleaf hash is
;   bd07f2eeb985e930ca48abb1a2169a565fba14758325a7077ed2b65065d9a856
;
; Run with
;   python3 examples/run-examples.py examples/test-commitment
; which checks every "; expect:" marker below, or interactively with
;   echo "import examples/test-commitment" | ./bllsh

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; context A: the valid spend, and the context it derives

spend 0  a08601000000000022512006e8b42f1b6e17f28cc00842fad5746a976c412892ca5ef7ba460e9385286d68
; expect: valid

; the spend set the introspection context as one derivation, and the
; executing program is the committed leaf: (tx 6) is its hash
blleval (= (tx (q . 6)) (q . 0xbd07f2eeb985e930ca48abb1a2169a565fba14758325a7077ed2b65065d9a856))
; expect: 1

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; context B: one signature bit flipped, the contract itself refuses

spend 0  a08601000000000022512006e8b42f1b6e17f28cc00842fad5746a976c412892ca5ef7ba460e9385286d68
; expect: invalid: ERR(bip340_verify: invalid, non-empty signature)

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; context C: the same signature encoded redundantly, refused at the
; boundary before evaluation, since a witness has one valid encoding

spend 0  a08601000000000022512006e8b42f1b6e17f28cc00842fad5746a976c412892ca5ef7ba460e9385286d68
; expect: invalid: environment: witness element not canonical: one byte atom with length prefix

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; context D: a fourth witness stack item, refused by the fixed layout
; so nobody can pad a third party's witness with extra items

spend 0  a08601000000000022512006e8b42f1b6e17f28cc00842fad5746a976c412892ca5ef7ba460e9385286d68
; expect: invalid: witness stack must be environment, leaf script, control block

; -------------------------------------------------------------------
; context E: the same program committed under leaf version 0xc0,
; which is a tapscript leaf, not a bll spend

spend 0  a08601000000000022512015febc787b4cce0995d430f19e51f95b1565e3f86b8c94a8f1d4428d900cb8e9
; expect: invalid: leaf version is not bll
